---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Site Notices" description="Privacy, cookie, terms of use, and copyright notices for the Teaching and Learning Mathematics Online companion site.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Site notices</p>
      <h1>The necessary small print.</h1>
      <p>This companion is intentionally simple. These notices explain what the site stores, what it measures, and who owns what.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow legal-copy">
      <section id="privacy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
        <h2>Analytics is optional.</h2>
        <p>This site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand broad patterns of use, such as which pages are visited and how readers move through the site. It uses measurement ID <code>G-FSDET4HG4L</code>, the same analytics property used by jameshoward.us.</p>
        <p>Google Analytics is not loaded until you explicitly accept analytics cookies. If you reject analytics, or if your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, the analytics tag remains disabled. The site does not use Google advertising signals or personalization features.</p>
        <p>When analytics is enabled, this site sends the page origin and path but deliberately excludes query strings from the page location supplied to Google Analytics.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies">
        <p class="eyebrow">Cookies and storage</p>
        <h2>One preference cookie; analytics only by consent.</h2>
        <p>The site stores one first-party preference cookie, <code>tlmo-consent</code>, so that it can remember whether you accepted or rejected optional analytics. The preference expires after one year.</p>
        <p>If analytics is accepted, Google Analytics may set cookies such as <code>_ga</code> and related identifiers. If analytics is later rejected, the site attempts to remove those analytics cookies and does not load the analytics tag on subsequent pages.</p>
        <p><button class="inline-settings-button" type="button" data-cookie-preferences>Open Cookie Settings</button></p>
      </section>

      <section id="terms">
        <p class="eyebrow">Terms of use</p>
        <h2>Use the site sensibly.</h2>
        <p>This website is an informational companion to <em>Teaching and Learning Mathematics Online</em>. It is provided as-is for educational and scholarly use. External links are provided for convenience and do not imply endorsement of every statement or service on an external site.</p>
        <p>Nothing on this site replaces the published text of either edition. Where bibliographic information differs from a publisher's current record, the publisher's record controls.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="copyright">
        <p class="eyebrow">Copyright</p>
        <h2>Site material and book material are not the same thing.</h2>
        <p>Copyright © 2020–{new Date().getFullYear()} James P. Howard, II and John F. Beyers. Site-original text, design, and teaching resources are reserved unless a page states otherwise.</p>
        <p>The books, chapter texts, cover art, publisher marks, and third-party logos remain subject to their respective copyrights, trademarks, licenses, and publisher terms.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
